   "stem": "In a proof by induction that $\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r = \\tfrac{n(n+1)}{2}$, the basis case $n=1$ has been checked. What is the **inductive step**?",
   "image": null,
   "options": [
    {
     "id": "A",
     "text": "Assume true for $n=k+1$, then show it is true for $n=k$.",
     "correct": false,
     "trap": "This goes backwards. You assume $n=k$ and prove $n=k+1$."
    },
    {
     "id": "B",
     "text": "Assume true for $n=k$, then show it is true for $n=k+1$.",
     "correct": true
    },
    {
     "id": "C",
     "text": "Check $n=1$ and $n=2$ only.",
     "correct": false,
     "trap": "Checking two cases is not a proof for every $n$."
    },
    {
     "id": "D",
     "text": "Assume the formula is true for every $n$.",
     "correct": false,
     "trap": "That assumes what you are trying to prove (circular)."
    }
